### IntelliJ HTTP Client - click the green arrow next to a request.
### Start the backend first (http://localhost:8080).

### 1. Public: list doctors
GET http://localhost:8080/api/doctors

### 2. Log in as the demo patient (saves the token for the next requests)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "patient@demo.com", "password": "demo123" }

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### 3. Who am I?
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Taken slots for doctor 1
GET http://localhost:8080/api/doctors/1/booked

### 5. Book an appointment (change the date: it must be a weekday the doctor works, within 60 days)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "doctorId": 1, "date": "2026-10-20", "time": "10:00", "reason": "Routine check-up" }

### 6. My appointments
GET http://localhost:8080/api/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Notifications
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
